; 21:2 ; 29:32-33 , 34 , 35 ; 30:5 , 7 (all J), 30:17 ; 30:19 ; 30:23 (all E), 38:3-4 , (both J), Exod 2:2 (E), 1Sam 1:20 ; 2:21 ; 2Kin 4:17 ; 1Chr 7:23 ; Isa 8:3 ; Hosea 1:3 , 6 , 8 , probably also 1Chr 4:17 אֶתמִֿרְיָם ותהר [ ותלד ] compare Be; further Judg 13:3 , and compare Moses' question יְלִדְתִּיהוּ אִםאָֿנֹכִי הַזֶּה כָּלהָֿעָם אֵת הָרִיתִי הֶאָנֹכִי Num 11:12 have I conceived all this people, or have I brought it forth? Participle f. || אֵם Hosea 2:7 ; Song 3:4 . 2 metaph . רוּחַ יָלַדְנוּ כְמוֺ חַלְנוּ הָרִינוּ Isa 26:18 of anxious and disappointed waiting; קַשׁ תֵּלְדוּ חֲשַׁשׁ תַּהֲרוּ 33:11 , of futile planning, compare Che; elsewhere of evil, mischief שָׁ֑קֶר וְיָלַד עָמָל וְהָרָה Psa 7:15 (subject wicked man), compare Job 15:35 ; Isa 59:4 , so also 59:13 , read הָרוֺ (Infinitive absolute) compare Di. Pu`al Perfect 3masculine singular נָּ֑בֶר הֹרָה Job 3:3 a man hath been conceived (Bö ii. p. 103 Ba NB 77 regard as Qal passive). Po. Infinitive absolute , conceive, contrive, devise שָׁ֑קֶר דִּבְרֵי מִלֵּב וְהֹגוֺ הֹרוֺ Isa 59:13 , but read rather וְהָגוֺ הָרוֺ Qal Infinitive absolute see above (Ba l.c. explanation ᵑ0 as Qal Infinitive passive ). — On הוֺרַי Gen 49:26 see הוֺר and הַר 1.c.","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 4 17","keyReferences":["1Chr 4 17","1Chr 7 23","1Sam 1 20","1Sam 2 21","2Kgs 4 17","2Sam 11 5","Exod 2 2","Gen 4 1"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":43,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 4 17","book":"1Chr","chapter":4,"verse":17,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/תַּ֨הַר֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3fs"},{"reference":"1Chr 7 23","book":"1Chr","chapter":7,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/תַּ֖הַר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3fs"},{"reference":"1Sam 1 20","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/תַּ֥הַר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3fs"